---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Todo from '../components/Todo.astro';
import { Content as Minutes } from '../data/minutes-2002.md';
import groupPhoto from '../assets/legacy/gfcbsg-group-photo-living-room.jpg';

const description =
  '大福克斯中文查经班的简介和历史：2002 年 10 月 20 日在北达科他大学国际中心成立。' +
  'About the Grand Forks Chinese Bible Study Group and its founding on October 20, 2002.';

// The archived 2002 meeting minutes are hidden for now. Change false to true
// to show them again; the text itself is in src/data/minutes-2002.md.
const showMinutes = false;
---

<Base title="关于我们 About" description={description}>
  <section class="container page-head">
    <h1 class="bi">
      <span lang="zh-Hans">关于我们</span>{' '}
      <span lang="en">About us</span>
    </h1>
    <div class="welcome-cols">
      <p lang="zh-Hans">
        大福克斯中文查经班（GFCBSG）是北达科他州大福克斯的一个中文查经班，成立于 2002
        年。多年来，我们一起查考圣经、聚餐，庆祝圣诞节和春节，也邀请讲员来分享。欢迎新老朋友！
      </p>
      <p lang="en">
        The Grand Forks Chinese Bible Study Group (GFCBSG) is a Chinese Bible study group in
        Grand Forks, North Dakota, founded in 2002. Over the years we have studied the Bible
        together, shared potluck dinners, celebrated Christmas and Chinese New Year, and welcomed
        guest speakers. Newcomers and old friends alike are welcome.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="history-title">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 id="history-title" class="bi section-head">
        <span lang="zh-Hans">我们的历史</span>{' '}
        <span lang="en">Our history</span>
      </h2>
      <div class="welcome-cols">
        <div lang="zh-Hans">
          <p>
            2002 年 10 月，北达科他大学校园举办了为期三天的福音聚会。聚会之后，2002 年 10 月 20
            日（星期日），查经班的筹备会议在北达科他大学国际中心召开。会议由 Abraham Hsueh
            牧师主持，他也应邀担任新成立的查经班的顾问。
          </p>
          <p>
            会上，与会者一一分享了参加福音聚会的感受和见证。Hsueh
            牧师勉励大家，并提出了三个步骤：第一，成立中文查经班，定期、系统地查考圣经；第二，建立教会，在本地区向华人广传福音；第三，寻找牧者牧养群羊。
          </p>
          <p>
            会议讨论了查经班的名称（UND-CBSG 或
            GGF-CBSG，当天没有作出最后决定），并推选了六位同工，首届任期六个月（2002 年 10 月至
            2003 年 4 月）。查经班定于每周五晚上 7 点到 9 点聚会，由四个家庭轮流开放家庭作为聚会地点。
          </p>
          <p>
            2002 年 11 月 1
            日，查经班举行了第一次查经（会议原定在 Chen 家举行）。按照计划，大家先用两周时间学习《创世记》前四章，之后查考《约翰福音》、《使徒行传》和《罗马书》。
          </p>
          <p>
            此后多年，查经班邀请了 Clement Yeung 医生、Chuck Kwok 博士、高德荣牧师（Pastor
            Ko）和庄祖鲲牧师等讲员来分享，举办聚餐、圣诞节和春节庆祝活动及见证分享，也接待了来访的短宣队。往年的活动记录请见<a
              href="/archive/">历年活动</a
            >。
          </p>
        </div>
        <div lang="en">
          <p>
            In October 2002, a three-day evangelical event was held on the University of North
            Dakota campus. Following it, on Sunday, October 20, 2002, an organizational meeting was
            held at the UND International Center. Rev. Abraham Hsueh facilitated the meeting and
            agreed to serve as the new group's consultant.
          </p>
          <p>
            One by one, the attendees shared their experiences and testimonies from the event.
            Rev. Hsueh encouraged them and set out three steps: first, establish a Chinese Bible
            study group and study the Bible regularly and systematically; second, plant a church
            and spread the gospel among Chinese people in the region; and third, find a pastor to
            shepherd the congregation.
          </p>
          <p>
            The meeting discussed a name for the group (UND-CBSG or GGF-CBSG; no final decision
            was made that day) and chose six coworkers for an initial six-month term, October 2002
            to April 2003. The group would meet every Friday night from 7 to 9 pm, rotating among
            four families who offered their homes.
          </p>
          <p>
            The first Bible study took place on November 1, 2002; the meeting had planned it for
            the Chen family's home. The plan was to spend two weeks on the first four chapters of
            Genesis, then study John, Acts and Romans.
          </p>
          <p>
            Over the years the group has welcomed guest speakers including Dr. Clement Yeung, Dr.
            Chuck Kwok, Pastor Ko and Pastor Tsu-Kung Chuang, shared potlucks, celebrated Christmas
            and Chinese New Year, heard testimonies, and hosted a visiting short-term mission team.
            See the <a href="/archive/">archive</a> for past events.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <figure class="photo">
        <Image
          src={groupPhoto}
          alt="Group photo of about 45 adults and children gathered in a living room"
        />
        <figcaption>
          <span lang="zh-Hans">查经班合影</span>{' '}
          <span lang="en">Group photo</span> ·{' '}
          <span lang="zh-Hans">日期</span>{' '}
          <span lang="en">Date:</span>
          <Todo />
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  {
    showMinutes && (
      <section class="section" aria-labelledby="minutes-title">
        <div class="container">
          <div class="section-head">
            <h2 id="minutes-title" class="bi">
              <span lang="zh-Hans">2002 年筹备会议记录</span>{' '}
              <span lang="en">Minutes of the 2002 organizational meeting</span>
            </h2>
            <p class="lead">
              <span lang="zh-Hans">以下是 2002 年 10 月 20 日筹备会议的原始记录（英文），由 Jean Chen 记录。</span>
              <br />
              <span lang="en">
                The original minutes of the organizational meeting on October 20, 2002, recorded by
                Jean Chen.
              </span>
            </p>
          </div>
          <article class="archive-doc" lang="en">
            <Minutes />
          </article>
          <aside class="note">
            <p>
              <span lang="zh-Hans">
                编者注：原文两处把“Hsueh”误拼为“Hsush”，已更正。另有姓名在原文中拼写不一致（Shu-Fen
                Shih / Shih-Fen Shih；Shen Yang / Yang Shen），保留原样。
              </span>
              <span lang="en">
                Editor's note: two misspellings of “Hsueh” as “Hsush” have been corrected. Some other
                names are spelled inconsistently in the original (Shu-Fen Shih / Shih-Fen Shih; Shen
                Yang / Yang Shen) and are left as written.
              </span>
              <span><Todo /></span>
            </p>
          </aside>
        </div>
      </section>
    )
  }
</Base>
